{
  "case_id": "2012-12-126",
  "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We're not dealing here with the situation where a prisoner is trying to gather new evidence AEDPA has a tolling rule to take care of that problem."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Bursch, I thought that -- that Perkins -- didn't he say that -- that you could take into account -- I'm looking for the brief -- you could take into account delay as a factor in whether his actual innocence gateway plea should be heard."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "got to act quickly, or adverse consequences can happen. But what diligence does that his rule doesn't do is it recognizes this compelling, countervailing State interest in having notice and an opportunity to investigate evidence, as soon as it's discovered."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If he gets close to the end of his year and he thinks that that next affidavit might be just around the corner, but he doesn't have it yet, all he has to do is file a protective habeas petition with the district court, ask for a stay, and say, I'm still diligently pursuing what I think is going to be another affidavit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the key difference between that scenario and the scenario that Perkins proposes is that, when you have him file something, the State's on notice, they have an opportunity to investigate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I have some difficulty understanding what the Sixth Circuit was doing. And maybe you can help me with that. The district court, as I understand it, said to the Petitioner, you lose for two reasons. First, you don't really have evidence of actual innocence, not enough anyway; and, second -- and I can understand that, because the evidence -- well, that -- the most that is suggested by the affidavits is that Jones was a participant in this murder, not that Perkins was not responsible for the murder."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0000-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They do say, in their opinion, that the case is remanded to the district court to determine whether he's got evidence of actual innocence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0000-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think that you should address the circuit split, which is the important question of do we apply the limitations period."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0000-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The analytical construct I want to set up is that we've got three different categories of prisoners who claim actual innocence, based on new evidence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amicus",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0000-0011",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In fact, if you look at the examples that the amici briefs cite on the Respondent's side, in almost every case, the final decision is motivated by State action."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0000-0014",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "both parties rely on that. The fact that you have an actual innocence exception only two subprovisions earlier is strong reason to think Congress didn't intend it here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Why does that make any sense?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bursch",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BURSCH: Because it was the Court itself that created the judicial exception to the State filing. And so then -- or, I'm sorry, that created the bar with respect to the State filing. And so then it was completely within the Court's power to make an exception to that bar."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Do you have any idea how many actual innocence claims win on the underlying constitutional issue?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0001-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF CHAD A. READLER ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Before you proceed with that, can you address Justice Alito's point that the district court said there is no merit to this; it's not an actual innocence -- it's not a valid actual innocence claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Readler",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. READLER: That's correct, Justice Ginsburg. And, with respect to Justice Alito's question, the reform recommendation from the magistrate denied this petition on statute of limitations grounds solely. It said it was too late, and it missed the statutory period."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Is that plausible, given what Congress was trying to do in AEDPA?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But, critically -- and I think my friend and I have a disagreement here -- critically, with respect to that provision, if you find evidence that solely goes to your innocence, that provision is not triggered, meaning you don't get another year if you find completely exculpatory evidence that shows you're not innocent, you don't -- you don't necessarily get another year."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: But that's very odd because, if you have somebody who's actually innocent, then you're saying that person can't get out of prison, unless the person happens to have a good constitutional claim that's totally unrelated to the fact that the person is actually innocent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Readler",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "MR. READLER: Well, I don't think so, Justice Alito, in the sense that all this is, is a gateway to allow them their first opportunity to bring a Federal habeas petition. Ordinarily, they're out of luck."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, assuming for the sake of argument that there is this exception, why shouldn't diligence be required? How can it be equitable to allow someone to bring a claim when the person has -- involving new evidence, when the person has not been diligent in presenting this new evidence to the court?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0002-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But the reason why is because, as Justice O'Connor said in her concurring opinion with -- with -- in Withrow, with Chief Justice Rehnquist, is that innocence is the ultimate equity. And it trumps -- diligence is not the ultimate equity, it's innocence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Are bribed jurors not a miscarriage of justice?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Yes, I mean, don't they toll it when there's some -- when the courthouse burns down?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Readler",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0002-0009",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And I think that's what should happen here for the -- for the first time, in our view. And there is a question -- there was a question, earlier, with respect to how often the Schlup standard is met. In response to the reply brief, we did a search of circuit courts. And we found, since Schlup was decided, eight circuits that have upheld or have found that Schlup was satisfied."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Readler",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't think it's one you can cast aside. I think you -- you have to give this more development. And, by the way, he was proceeding pro se. I think, when he -- when the case is remanded, with assistance of counsel, he can present -- better present the evidence and better present some other things, to make -- make the showing stronger. And I think we can meet the Schlup standard."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "John J. Bursch",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "With respect to Holland, I want to note, first of all, that, there, you were dealing with legislative silence. Everyone agreed that Congress had not said anything about equitable tolling."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "John J. Bursch",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And, as I explained earlier, when you consider the three categories of defendants who claim actual innocence based on new evidence, this situation here, where the new evidence relates to the factual predicate of the constitutional claim asserted, that's where Congress, most clearly, meant to have the limitations period apply."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "General, you had suggested, earlier, some way out of this puzzle about why Congress would have put the actual innocence exception into the second successive petition provision and not had one for a first petition?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "John J. Bursch",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What they did in 2244(d)(1)(D) is they made it broader. They said, even if you don't claim innocence, if you are coming forward with new evidence, we want the court to hear that constitutional claim, if you bring it within one year."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "John J. Bursch",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0003-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "you are stuck with (d)(1)(D), you have got to file within a year. All that the successive petition adds to it is that you do have a statutory actual innocence gateway to pass through first that you don't have on your first petition. That's our position."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2012-12-126",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3ffda61a2fb2e27862eb7f23544fc1f0182789d2dd77a7c10c7c3ac7fa4bb1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3ffda61a2f-0003-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What do you think about the words \"discovered in exercise of due diligence\"?"
